    "agrees": true,
    "note": "Hashes were downloaded from the published v5.27.1 release assets and hashed independently, then checked again by re-fetching the URL this pin itself names. v5.27.1 fixes one sentence the v5.27.0 reconversion left unswept: the graph server convention section for the teaching voice still told it that, when that convention file is unreadable, it should read the files themselves -- calling that the one discovery tool the voice is granted. True while the voice declared only read; since the reconversion it has read, grep and glob, so the sentence told it its only recourse was reading, in exactly the situation the reconversion existed to fix. The permission was always right; what was wrong was what the prompt told the voice it had. The fix is not a corrected count: the sentence went stale because it enumerated a capability, so it no longer does -- it names the fallback by what it is for, which cannot age the next time the toolbox changes. Found by reading the prompt as installed on a real machine, after the suite was green and a fresh-context review had passed; neither checks whether a convention prose still agrees with the agent declared tools. Only the pegasus artifact changed; install.sh and the two builder scripts are byte-identical to v5.25.1."
  }
